1
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,271
<i>Hey, this is Houston.
Do you copy?</i>

2
00:01:15,396 --> 00:01:16,355
Copy Houston.

3
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,479
<i>It's Christy. How's it going?</i>

4
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,230
Hey, Christy,
it's great to hear your voice.

5
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,687
<i>Sam's family wants
to connect with her immediately.</i>

6
00:01:22,688 --> 00:01:23,645
<i>Is she nearby?</i>

7
00:01:23,646 --> 00:01:25,145
She's in the research facility.

8
00:01:25,146 --> 00:01:27,105
- I'll just connect to her.
<i>- Okay, copy!</i>

9
00:01:39,355 --> 00:01:41,313
Sam, you got a call from India.

10
00:02:03,063 --> 00:02:04,896
<i>Your call has been forwarded to a--</i>

11
00:02:05,896 --> 00:02:08,146
- Brother!
- Hello! Welcome, in-laws.

12
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:10,813
Son-in-law hasn't…

13
00:02:10,938 --> 00:02:12,688
He's on the flight over here.

14
00:02:13,146 --> 00:02:14,770
"Has Adhithi eaten?
Did Adhithi get some sleep?

15
00:02:14,771 --> 00:02:17,271
Did Adhithi like the arrangements?
Did she like the handloom sari?"

16
00:02:17,396 --> 00:02:18,938
In fact, he even inquired about you.

17
00:02:19,188 --> 00:02:20,395
Oh, that's sweet of him.

18
00:02:20,396 --> 00:02:22,855
You don't worry about anything.
I'll handle everything.

19
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:24,188
He will be here on time.

20
00:02:24,771 --> 00:02:25,813
Why don't you have a drink with me?

21
00:02:26,021 --> 00:02:27,521
It's okay, not now.
You carry on!

22
00:02:27,771 --> 00:02:28,688
Let's go!

23
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:31,230
<i>That was a close call!</i>

24
00:02:35,105 --> 00:02:37,020
- Come here, damn it!
- Come dance with me, Uncle.

25
00:02:37,021 --> 00:02:38,520
You're dancing unaware of the situation.

26
00:02:38,521 --> 00:02:39,605
And you're inviting me on top of it.

27
00:02:39,771 --> 00:02:41,063
Uncle, he did call, right?

28
00:02:41,855 --> 00:02:44,270
No one has been answering my calls.
How many times should I call them?

29
00:02:44,271 --> 00:02:46,230
- When did you call them?
- Since this morning.

30
00:02:46,355 --> 00:02:47,563
If it's morning here,
it's night out there.

31
00:02:47,813 --> 00:02:50,063
It is only dawn for them now.
Uncle, call them now.

32
00:03:03,938 --> 00:03:04,895
Hello?

33
00:03:04,896 --> 00:03:06,438
Sachin, why aren't you answering my calls?

34
00:03:06,605 --> 00:03:08,520
- Who are you?
- Huh? FBI!

35
00:03:08,521 --> 00:03:10,813
- Haven't you left for the wedding yet?
- Who is getting married?

36
00:03:11,146 --> 00:03:12,645
Bloody sinners! Are you guys drunk?

37
00:03:12,646 --> 00:03:13,563
Uncle!

38
00:03:13,938 --> 00:03:14,937
<i>What are you guys doing?</i>

39
00:03:14,938 --> 00:03:17,354
<i>The wedding is tomorrow. And I don't
see that you guys are serious about it.</i>

40
00:03:17,355 --> 00:03:18,521
<i>Is this how you behave?</i>

41
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:20,896
How could you guys be so irresponsible?

42
00:03:21,355 --> 00:03:22,562
Everyone here is stressed out.

43
00:03:22,563 --> 00:03:24,146
For God's sake, get here soon.
Please!

44
00:03:24,313 --> 00:03:26,980
Uncle, it's my responsibility
to bring Idhaya to the wedding.

45
00:03:27,105 --> 00:03:28,271
Please hang up.

46
00:03:28,688 --> 00:03:29,980
- Hey, where's Idhaya?
- Idhaya?

47
00:03:30,146 --> 00:03:31,063
Idhaya!

48
00:03:31,188 --> 00:03:32,938
Where the hell is Idhaya?
Idhaya!

49
00:03:33,063 --> 00:03:34,563
- Hey, Idhaya?
- Let me check upstairs.

50
00:03:34,688 --> 00:03:35,688
- Idhaya!
- Idhaya!

51
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:37,146
Hey!

52
00:03:41,646 --> 00:03:44,063
<i>O Heart of mine</i>

53
00:03:45,771 --> 00:03:47,896
Oh, my God! Look at him.

54
00:03:48,938 --> 00:03:50,771
We're getting late for the flight.
Why aren't you guys ready yet?

55
00:03:52,188 --> 00:03:53,980
Buddy, that's the spirit!

56
00:03:54,896 --> 00:03:57,021
- My best friend is getting married.
- Yay!

57
00:03:57,146 --> 00:03:58,187
What are you guys waiting for?

58
00:03:58,188 --> 00:03:59,812
We only have
two hours for the flight. Scram!

59
00:03:59,813 --> 00:04:01,521
Oh, damn, let's get ready soon.

60
00:04:01,896 --> 00:04:04,730
<i>I've found my way to you</i>

61
00:04:05,605 --> 00:04:07,980
Instead of packing,
why are you throwing it down?

62
00:04:08,271 --> 00:04:10,105
Quickly pack up. We're getting late.

63
00:04:12,355 --> 00:04:13,730
Hey, throw that away.

64
00:04:15,771 --> 00:04:16,687
Here you go!

65
00:04:16,688 --> 00:04:22,313
<i>Your misguided thoughts
Left me drowning in sorrow</i>

66
00:04:22,521 --> 00:04:27,896
<i>Like nectar in every flower,
My heart seeks you every day</i>

67
00:04:39,521 --> 00:04:42,230
<i>Butterflies are fluttering</i>

68
00:04:42,438 --> 00:04:45,188
<i>A game of hide-and-seek is on</i>

69
00:04:45,313 --> 00:04:47,855
<i>Everything looks lush and green</i>

70
00:04:48,021 --> 00:04:50,771
<i>Everything looks lush and green</i>

71
00:04:50,896 --> 00:04:53,605
<i>Butterflies are fluttering</i>

72
00:04:53,813 --> 00:04:56,480
<i>A game of hide-and-seek is on</i>

73
00:04:56,730 --> 00:04:59,355
<i>Everything looks lush and green</i>

74
00:04:59,605 --> 00:05:04,313
<i>Beautiful birds circle in our sight</i>

75
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,896
<i>O Heart of mine</i>

76
00:05:08,438 --> 00:05:11,230
<i>You're one of a kind</i>

77
00:05:11,396 --> 00:05:13,646
<i>O Heart of mine</i>

78
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,730
<i>My throbbing love</i>

79
00:05:26,688 --> 00:05:27,938
Hey, you work out, right?

80
00:05:28,105 --> 00:05:29,604
- Hand it to me.
- Thanks!

81
00:05:29,605 --> 00:05:31,812
- Where's the huge bag?
- Hey, I did not bring it.

82
00:05:31,813 --> 00:05:33,980
- You never asked me to.
- Why do you do this, Priya?

83
00:05:34,146 --> 00:05:36,813
I regret bringing you guys
on business class.

84
00:05:37,230 --> 00:05:38,770
- Oh, God!
- Sir, please sit down.

85
00:05:38,771 --> 00:05:40,438
- Aren't they supposed to serve us juice?
- Sir, please sit down.

86
00:05:40,563 --> 00:05:41,770
Ma'am, please!

87
00:05:41,771 --> 00:05:44,479
- Hey, where are you going?
- I'm going to the loo.

88
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:46,104
- Do I need permission for it?
- Prabhu, go with him.

89
00:05:46,105 --> 00:05:47,771
- He might jump off the plane.
- Two cannot fit in there.

90
00:05:47,938 --> 00:05:48,938
Fine, I'll adjust

91
00:05:52,521 --> 00:05:54,021
<i>Hey, fool! Fool!</i>

92
00:05:54,355 --> 00:05:55,645
<i>- Did you board the flight or not?</i>
- What?

93
00:05:55,646 --> 00:05:57,688
<i>Bloody dirty pants.
Peg yourself to be a great actor?</i>

94
00:06:00,188 --> 00:06:01,437
- Hello?
<i>- I'll rip you apart.</i>

95
00:06:01,438 --> 00:06:03,605
<i>What's with the hello?
The wedding is tomorrow!</i>

96
00:06:03,771 --> 00:06:05,770
<i>If you don't make it here,
you're as good as dead.</i>

97
00:06:05,771 --> 00:06:07,105
<i>Send me a picture of you
sitting on the flight.</i>

98
00:06:07,313 --> 00:06:08,646
<i>If the wedding gets called off…</i>

99
00:06:17,355 --> 00:06:18,271
Give me the phone.

100
00:06:19,230 --> 00:06:20,146
Phone?

101
00:06:20,813 --> 00:06:22,230
I can't give you my phone, sir.

102
00:06:22,521 --> 00:06:23,813
It contains a lot of personal information.

103
00:06:24,646 --> 00:06:27,230
I don't want your phone.
Give me back my phone.

104
00:06:30,563 --> 00:06:33,313
I'm so sorry.
Same phone and same color.

105
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:38,230
Is your uncle very short-tempered?

106
00:06:39,896 --> 00:06:42,396
Uncle?
Did my uncle call?

107
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:46,355
Did you answer the call?

108
00:06:47,146 --> 00:06:48,563
He yelled at me in colorful words.

109
00:06:49,105 --> 00:06:51,771
He said he'd kill you if you didn't
make it to the wedding tomorrow.

110
00:06:52,521 --> 00:06:55,313
Sir, ask him why he's here
when his wedding is tomorrow.

111
00:06:56,896 --> 00:06:57,813
I understand!

112
00:06:58,188 --> 00:07:00,938
You're looking for a scapegoat
to narrate your flashback.

113
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,604
- Am I right?
- No, sir.

114
00:07:02,605 --> 00:07:04,604
I'm not the man for it.
Please find someone else.

115
00:07:04,605 --> 00:07:06,104
- Sir, the others here are foreigners.
- Yes, sir.

116
00:07:06,105 --> 00:07:08,230
Our story is rooted in the native.
Only you'd be the right match.

117
00:07:08,396 --> 00:07:09,646
I'm going to watch TV.

118
00:07:09,855 --> 00:07:13,021
Sir, they offered an $800 coupon
because the TV is not working.

119
00:07:13,146 --> 00:07:14,187
Didn't they offer you?

120
00:07:14,188 --> 00:07:15,813
It's okay. I'll read a book.

121
00:07:17,230 --> 00:07:19,146
Sir, that's a guide manual.

122
00:07:19,646 --> 00:07:21,854
You have no choice
but to listen to our story.

123
00:07:21,855 --> 00:07:22,854
- Yes, sir.
- Sir,

124
00:07:22,855 --> 00:07:24,687
you're tailored to listen
to a flashback.

125
00:07:24,688 --> 00:07:27,438
Wearing shades, a suit,
and sitting next to us.

126
00:07:27,646 --> 00:07:30,020
Sir, it's a love story.
And it's very interesting.

127
00:07:30,021 --> 00:07:32,979
It'll be a time-pass for you.
And a venting session for us.

128
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:35,646
Sir, even the supporting
actor has two love stories.

129
00:07:35,771 --> 00:07:37,188
- Hear us out, sir.
- Yes, sir.

130
00:07:37,355 --> 00:07:38,271
What's the run-time?

131
00:07:38,521 --> 00:07:41,021
Sir, the first half runs
for 1 hour and 23 minutes.

132
00:07:41,146 --> 00:07:43,145
But the second half is trimmed
to 1 hour and 20 minutes.

133
00:07:43,146 --> 00:07:45,271
Sir, we can complete the movie
within 2 hours and 43 minutes.

134
00:07:45,521 --> 00:07:46,688
Start the film, guys!

135
00:08:09,188 --> 00:08:10,813
<i>We're a mix of 80s and 90s kids.</i>

136
00:08:11,730 --> 00:08:14,521
<i>We're the last chapter
of a slower, gentler world.</i>

137
00:08:14,730 --> 00:08:18,063
<i>Before the world began to race,
even doing nothing felt like happiness.</i>

138
00:08:18,271 --> 00:08:20,271
<i>Back then, happiness was simple.</i>

139
00:08:20,563 --> 00:08:22,605
<i>Lying on the rooftop, gazing at the sky.</i>

140
00:08:22,896 --> 00:08:24,896
<i>Even though it's not much,
our hearts were lighter.</i>

141
00:08:25,188 --> 00:08:28,063
<i>Friends were not profile pictures
or status updates.</i>

142
00:08:28,188 --> 00:08:30,438
<i>But the one who knocks on the door
to call out to play.</i>

143
00:08:30,688 --> 00:08:32,980
<i>No cafe latte or filter coffees.</i>

144
00:08:33,355 --> 00:08:35,521
<i>Five bucks Popsicle,
and two bags of Lays.</i>

145
00:08:35,688 --> 00:08:36,813
<i>That was our world.</i>

146
00:08:37,938 --> 00:08:41,771
<i>Even cycling felt like
we were the King and Queen.</i>

147
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:44,645
<i>When the street lights come on,
it's time to get back home.</i>

148
00:08:44,646 --> 00:08:46,063
<i>The lights coming on were our deadline.</i>

149
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:48,730
<i>But the same lights
were our childhood guardian.</i>

150
00:08:49,146 --> 00:08:52,355
<i>When technology advanced,
we embraced and adjusted to it.</i>

151
00:08:52,688 --> 00:08:55,980
<i>Right from the ringing of landlines
to this generation's seen status.</i>

152
00:08:56,105 --> 00:08:58,105
<i>But our world wasn't a virtual one.</i>

153
00:08:58,438 --> 00:09:00,105
<i>The scent of rain and sand,</i>

154
00:09:00,438 --> 00:09:02,730
<i>open playgrounds,
our mother's voice calling out to us…</i>

155
00:09:03,063 --> 00:09:04,271
<i>Those were our ring-tones.</i>

156
00:09:04,688 --> 00:09:07,105
<i>Back then, life wasn't loud but light.</i>

157
00:09:10,021 --> 00:09:11,896
<i>We're bearing both versions of the world.</i>

158
00:09:12,188 --> 00:09:15,813
<i>From the time when VHS tapes
gave us irreplaceable memories.</i>

159
00:09:16,563 --> 00:09:17,855
<i>We'll never get those days back.</i>

160
00:09:18,063 --> 00:09:19,980
<i>However, it hasn't left us.</i>

161
00:09:20,230 --> 00:09:21,646
<i>They're still alive in us.</i>

162
00:09:21,855 --> 00:09:24,105
<i>It's alive in our smile, memories…</i>

163
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:27,605
<i>That indescribable feeling
when an old song slows your heartbeat.</i>

164
00:09:34,063 --> 00:09:35,855
<i>We're the last simple generation.</i>

165
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:38,605
<i>But we're the first magic generation.</i>

166
00:09:49,063 --> 00:09:51,771
Hey, Idhaya, hot water is ready.
Quickly take a shower.

167
00:09:51,938 --> 00:09:54,521
Uncle, let me watch some more TV
and then take a shower.

168
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:57,062
How long will you wear these dirty pants
without taking a shower?

169
00:09:57,063 --> 00:09:59,480
- Uncle, let me watch TV for some time.
- Stop watching TV up close.

170
00:10:00,021 --> 00:10:01,230
<i>I don't have parents.</i>

171
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:03,313
<i>But I have my uncle.</i>

172
00:10:03,938 --> 00:10:05,146
<i>He's everything for me.</i>

173
00:10:07,396 --> 00:10:08,355
Why are you guys late?

174
00:10:08,521 --> 00:10:10,063
- I woke up late, dude.
- Run! Run!

175
00:10:10,313 --> 00:10:12,104
- Me too.
- Once again, they're late to school.

176
00:10:12,105 --> 00:10:13,021
- Come.
- Sir!

177
00:10:13,313 --> 00:10:15,855
The last bell has rung,
and everyone is rushing in.

178
00:10:16,021 --> 00:10:18,271
But you guys are happily taking your time.

179
00:10:20,188 --> 00:10:22,730
<i>In our school lives,
we all have one favorite teacher.</i>

180
00:10:23,021 --> 00:10:25,271
<i>Affectionate, caring, and close to us.</i>

181
00:10:25,521 --> 00:10:26,938
<i>Yes, beautiful, too.</i>

182
00:10:27,438 --> 00:10:29,188
<i>And that's what
Geetha teacher meant to me.</i>

183
00:10:29,521 --> 00:10:30,730
<i>My English teacher.</i>

184
00:10:51,896 --> 00:10:54,730
Prabhu, my tooth came off.

185
00:10:55,521 --> 00:10:58,396
Then rush and bury it
without anyone knowing.

186
00:10:58,521 --> 00:10:59,438
Why?

187
00:10:59,813 --> 00:11:01,646
Only then will a new tooth grow.

188
00:11:02,063 --> 00:11:03,271
Are you guys telling the truth?

189
00:11:03,813 --> 00:11:05,562
Why? Aren't you aware of it?

190
00:11:05,563 --> 00:11:06,480
I don't know.

191
00:11:10,021 --> 00:11:13,521
Hey, don't eat the seeds.
A tree will grow inside your stomach.

192
00:11:15,355 --> 00:11:16,480
Are you guys telling the truth?

193
00:11:16,771 --> 00:11:20,146
- Hey, he's got twin swirls on his head.
- Yes!

194
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:22,688
That means he'll marry two wives.

195
00:11:23,396 --> 00:11:24,771
Are you guys telling the truth?

196
00:11:27,230 --> 00:11:28,520
Good morning, students!

197
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:31,021
Good morning, teacher!

198
00:11:32,605 --> 00:11:36,563
In this year's annual day event,
who is willing to participate?

199
00:11:37,063 --> 00:11:39,480
Hey, don't raise your hands.

200
00:11:39,688 --> 00:11:41,521
It'll be humiliating on the stage.

201
00:11:44,563 --> 00:11:45,563
Idhaya!

202
00:11:46,813 --> 00:11:49,063
- Aren't you interested?
- I'm interested, Teacher.

203
00:11:51,605 --> 00:11:52,521
Good!

204
00:11:53,855 --> 00:11:55,771
Even Prabhu and Dravid are interested.

205
00:12:00,355 --> 00:12:01,271
Very good!

206
00:12:04,563 --> 00:12:07,063
- Check if it's clear now.
- Hey, is the transmission clear?

207
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:08,896
No!

208
00:12:09,146 --> 00:12:10,771
It's not clear yet, Uncle!

209
00:12:12,063 --> 00:12:12,980
Wait a minute!

210
00:12:16,021 --> 00:12:17,021
It must be clear now.

211
00:12:18,730 --> 00:12:19,646
Now?

212
00:12:29,146 --> 00:12:31,021
What are they doing, guys?

213
00:12:31,396 --> 00:12:34,188
They're planning to have a baby.

214
00:12:34,688 --> 00:12:36,313
How do you know about this?

215
00:12:36,563 --> 00:12:39,396
Didn't you see them kiss?

216
00:12:39,688 --> 00:12:40,605
Hey, Idhaya!

217
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,355
So what if they kissed?

218
00:12:42,563 --> 00:12:45,354
Don't you know
that kissing can lead to pregnancy?

219
00:12:45,355 --> 00:12:46,730
Are you guys telling the truth?

220
00:12:46,855 --> 00:12:48,605
Aren't you aware of it?

221
00:12:48,813 --> 00:12:50,188
No, I know about it.

222
00:12:50,730 --> 00:12:52,688
Still, let's clarify with brother Sachin.

223
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:55,605
You're right.
Brother will give us clarity.

224
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,646
That's right, guys!

225
00:12:57,855 --> 00:13:00,438
Kissing will lead to pregnancy.
Don't you guys know?

226
00:13:00,646 --> 00:13:03,395
I'm ashamed to call you guys my juniors.

227
00:13:03,396 --> 00:13:04,312
Damn!

228
00:13:04,313 --> 00:13:05,855
How would we know, brother?

229
00:13:06,855 --> 00:13:08,230
That's why we came to you.

230
00:13:08,355 --> 00:13:10,605
I have to teach you guys everything.

231
00:13:10,730 --> 00:13:12,438
Fine, there's nothing I can do about it.

232
00:13:12,646 --> 00:13:13,980
Because you're like
younger brothers to me.

233
00:13:14,813 --> 00:13:17,770
Now we're going to witness
the fancy dress competition

234
00:13:17,771 --> 00:13:21,271
of our 1998 Annual Day celebration.

235
00:13:21,563 --> 00:13:24,021
First of all,
we're welcoming The Hanuman.

236
00:13:31,063 --> 00:13:33,355
Good evening, I'm Abraham Lincoln.

237
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:36,813
I'm the 16th President
of the United States of America.

238
00:13:37,105 --> 00:13:38,021
Thank you.

239
00:13:38,813 --> 00:13:41,479
Hello, everyone!
I'm Netaji Subash Chandra Bose.

240
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,979
A freedom fighter of India.

241
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:43,896
Jai Hind!

242
00:13:48,896 --> 00:13:51,563
I am… Neil Armstrong…

243
00:13:53,688 --> 00:13:54,646
I am…

244
00:13:56,646 --> 00:13:57,563
I am…

245
00:13:59,896 --> 00:14:00,813
Neil…

246
00:14:03,396 --> 00:14:04,646
Armstrong…

247
00:14:06,355 --> 00:14:07,271
Idhaya!

248
00:14:08,313 --> 00:14:09,230
Idhaya!

249
00:14:12,563 --> 00:14:13,563
What happened?

250
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:16,646
I'm right here beside you.

251
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,688
Speak confidently.

252
00:14:23,396 --> 00:14:25,146
That's a small step for a man.

253
00:14:25,605 --> 00:14:27,730
One giant leap for mankind.

254
00:14:41,188 --> 00:14:43,688
You spoke brilliantly, Idhaya.
It was amazing.

255
00:14:45,730 --> 00:14:46,688
Thank you, Teacher.

256
00:15:01,021 --> 00:15:03,896
<i>Don't you know
that kissing can lead to pregnancy?</i>

257
00:15:20,646 --> 00:15:21,605
Uncle!

258
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:25,729
How are babies born?

259
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:26,688
Hey, dirty pants!

260
00:15:26,938 --> 00:15:29,063
Holy shit! What are you saying?

261
00:15:29,521 --> 00:15:31,563
Idhaya, it's a very big mistake.

262
00:15:33,021 --> 00:15:34,395
Shall we start from one?

263
00:15:34,396 --> 00:15:36,063
<i>- So, I was scared since then…</i>
- One.

264
00:15:36,855 --> 00:15:39,562
<i>…thinking if Geetha teacher's stomach
will start growing.</i>

265
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:40,563
Nothing, Teacher.

266
00:15:47,646 --> 00:15:48,896
You're behind three months.

267
00:15:51,188 --> 00:15:53,146
- Hey, hold the baby for me.
- I won't!

268
00:15:53,271 --> 00:15:54,188
Hey, hold the baby!

269
00:15:54,563 --> 00:15:56,062
Hey, Idhaya!
Why is he running scared?

270
00:15:56,063 --> 00:15:56,980
Hey, it's raining!

271
00:16:09,896 --> 00:16:11,646
Good morning! Good morning!

272
00:16:11,855 --> 00:16:13,438
Good morning, Teacher!

273
00:16:13,563 --> 00:16:15,605
How were your summer holidays?

274
00:16:16,396 --> 00:16:18,688
You guys are no longer in your 4th grade

275
00:16:18,896 --> 00:16:20,646
but you have graduated to the 5th grade.

276
00:16:21,688 --> 00:16:24,479
<i>I was scared after looking
at Geetha teacher's stomach.</i>

277
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:28,646
This year we have a new student
in our class.

278
00:16:30,146 --> 00:16:33,396
<i>In that moment, I decided that
Geetha teacher's child is my child.</i>

279
00:16:33,605 --> 00:16:34,896
<i>It's our child.</i>

280
00:16:35,730 --> 00:16:38,895
<i>I decided to take care
of her and the child.</i>

281
00:16:38,896 --> 00:16:39,854
May I help you?

282
00:16:39,855 --> 00:16:41,563
- Oh, do you want to help me?
- Yes!

283
00:16:42,188 --> 00:16:43,105
Okay.

284
00:17:34,105 --> 00:17:35,105
Hey, let's go inside.

285
00:17:35,938 --> 00:17:37,271
Teacher, what happened to you?

286
00:17:37,771 --> 00:17:39,770
- What happened?
- Please call for an auto.

287
00:17:39,771 --> 00:17:40,771
Idhaya, hurry up!

288
00:17:47,855 --> 00:17:50,063
Auto! Auto!

289
00:17:51,646 --> 00:17:52,646
Please help me.

290
00:17:53,938 --> 00:17:54,855
What happened, son?

291
00:17:55,021 --> 00:17:56,938
She's in labor.
We have to go to the hospital.

292
00:17:57,063 --> 00:17:58,563
Is it your mother?

293
00:17:59,688 --> 00:18:01,145
- No!
- Then who?

294
00:18:01,146 --> 00:18:02,313
- Idhaya!
- Teacher!

295
00:18:04,605 --> 00:18:05,521
I'm coming, ma'am.

296
00:18:06,855 --> 00:18:07,855
You'll be fine, Teacher!

297
00:18:08,021 --> 00:18:09,021
Be careful…

298
00:18:11,230 --> 00:18:13,270
Nurse!
Bring a gurney, it's an emergency.

299
00:18:13,271 --> 00:18:14,896
- Teacher, please don't fear.
- Hold the umbrella.

300
00:18:15,021 --> 00:18:16,230
Come on, hurry up!

301
00:18:30,646 --> 00:18:31,937
Brother, where can I find a phone?

302
00:18:31,938 --> 00:18:33,063
Go straight and take the last right.

303
00:19:01,896 --> 00:19:04,813
Kids, I've informed your teacher's family.

304
00:19:05,105 --> 00:19:06,271
They'll be here soon.

305
00:19:06,521 --> 00:19:08,646
Your folks must be looking for you guys.
Let's go.

306
00:19:09,438 --> 00:19:12,563
I appreciate it.
You guys did so much for your teacher.

307
00:19:12,855 --> 00:19:14,146
It's not for our teacher.

308
00:19:16,271 --> 00:19:17,646
But for his wife.

309
00:19:20,438 --> 00:19:22,605
Almost everyone in this world
has had a crush on a teacher.

310
00:19:23,355 --> 00:19:25,896
That's the inception of unrequited love.

311
00:19:29,271 --> 00:19:30,605
Fine, let's go home.

312
00:19:38,063 --> 00:19:41,438
Hey, why is he getting emotional
like 'Idhayam' Murali?

313
00:19:42,396 --> 00:19:43,438
Hey!

314
00:19:45,646 --> 00:19:48,355
Let's go. There'll be more things
in life to get emotional about.

315
00:19:49,396 --> 00:19:50,313
Get in!

316
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,521
<i>After that,
I never saw Geetha teacher.</i>

317
00:19:55,021 --> 00:19:57,271
<i>I was told that she quit her job
and moved to another city.</i>

318
00:19:57,938 --> 00:20:00,063
<i>That was the last day
I saw Geetha teacher.</i>

319
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:06,230
Where was her husband
while you were signing the form?

320
00:20:06,396 --> 00:20:08,646
Sir, he was a sincere shepherd.

321
00:20:08,855 --> 00:20:10,855
He was abroad herding white sheep.

322
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:13,105
He left a pregnant woman alone
on the verge of delivery.

323
00:20:13,313 --> 00:20:14,855
He must be a classic jerk.

324
00:20:15,771 --> 00:20:17,188
Indeed, he's a jerk.

325
00:20:17,313 --> 00:20:20,605
Sir, after that breakup, his tender
heart was torn into many pieces.

326
00:20:21,021 --> 00:20:21,980
I understood!

327
00:20:22,355 --> 00:20:24,312
Leave out love stories
that didn't work out.

328
00:20:24,313 --> 00:20:25,980
Just narrate the ones that worked out.

329
00:20:26,355 --> 00:20:29,355
<i>Today, we'll be discussing corrosion.</i>

330
00:20:29,563 --> 00:20:32,480
You must be familiar
with the rusting of iron.

331
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:35,062
Green patches on a copper vessel.

332
00:20:35,063 --> 00:20:36,646
And brass vessels.

333
00:20:41,271 --> 00:20:42,188
Hey!

334
00:20:42,605 --> 00:20:44,938
- The bell will ring, right?
- Yes, it will ring.

335
00:20:45,271 --> 00:20:46,230
What if it's broken?

336
00:20:46,563 --> 00:20:47,605
I will ring it myself.

337
00:20:48,605 --> 00:20:51,146
…most commonly with oxygen.

338
00:20:52,271 --> 00:20:53,271
Sit down, please.

339
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:55,480
Let me finish my explanation.

340
00:20:55,646 --> 00:20:57,605
Then I can allow you to go.

341
00:20:57,938 --> 00:21:00,270
Corrosion is a natural process.

342
00:21:00,271 --> 00:21:01,896
Hey, will he let us go or not?

343
00:21:02,063 --> 00:21:04,771
Hey, he'll let us go.
Be patient for five minutes.

344
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:07,105
…stable chemical state.

345
00:21:08,271 --> 00:21:09,855
Please stand for the prayer.

346
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,855
- Our Father…
- Our Father…

347
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:14,395
- …who art in heaven…
- …who art in heaven…

348
00:21:14,396 --> 00:21:17,020
- …lead us not into temptation…
- …lead us not into temptation…

349
00:21:17,021 --> 00:21:19,437
- …but deliver us from evil.
- …but deliver us from evil.

350
00:21:19,438 --> 00:21:20,605
- Amen!
- Amen!

351
00:21:20,730 --> 00:21:23,021
Okay, boys! See you all tomorrow.

352
00:21:23,605 --> 00:21:24,980
Where is he rushing off to?

353
00:21:36,188 --> 00:21:37,188
Who is he?

354
00:21:37,521 --> 00:21:38,980
Where does he go with him every evening?

355
00:21:39,313 --> 00:21:40,813
He comes to pick him up daily.

356
00:21:47,021 --> 00:21:48,771
Dude, he's having something.

357
00:21:51,688 --> 00:21:54,021
- Let's inquire what's happening.
- Hey, don't go.

358
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:55,813
He looks dangerous.

359
00:21:56,688 --> 00:21:57,605
Don't be scared!

360
00:21:57,771 --> 00:21:58,979
Hey, I'm running away.

361
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:00,812
Hey, he's looking at us.
Let's go away.

362
00:22:00,813 --> 00:22:02,646
Hey, turn around casually.
Let's go.

363
00:22:02,813 --> 00:22:03,812
Why are you scared of him?

364
00:22:03,813 --> 00:22:05,563
- We're getting late.
- Hey, I was praying for us.

365
00:22:05,771 --> 00:22:06,896
Ride faster.

366
00:22:13,438 --> 00:22:14,521
- Idhaya!
- Coming!

367
00:22:14,688 --> 00:22:15,604
Bye, Uncle.

368
00:22:15,605 --> 00:22:17,563
Don't go on an empty stomach.
At least have some tea.

369
00:22:18,688 --> 00:22:19,688
Oh, no!

370
00:22:20,605 --> 00:22:22,105
- I'm getting late, Uncle.
- Stop acting. Come here.

371
00:22:26,771 --> 00:22:28,480
Two things I love the most in this world.

372
00:22:28,730 --> 00:22:30,563
- One is your tea.
- What's the second one?

373
00:22:31,438 --> 00:22:33,313
- Dude, come on!
- Oh, no!

374
00:22:33,938 --> 00:22:34,855
I won't reveal it.

375
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:37,437
- Love you. Bye, Uncle.
- Hey! Hey! Hey!

376
00:22:37,438 --> 00:22:39,021
Hey, reveal it.

377
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:41,937
In the evening, we have practice.
Don't forget.

378
00:22:41,938 --> 00:22:42,895
We have a match coming up.

379
00:22:42,896 --> 00:22:44,145
- Hey, I have to go.
- Bye!

380
00:22:44,146 --> 00:22:45,396
Dravid, bye! Prabhu, bye!

381
00:22:46,313 --> 00:22:47,438
{\an8}Bye, guys! Bye, bye, bye!

382
00:23:00,146 --> 00:23:01,063
Idhaya.

383
00:23:02,063 --> 00:23:04,396
- Hi, guys! When did you come?
- Just now.

384
00:23:05,271 --> 00:23:06,271
Meet my friend, Juju.

385
00:23:07,105 --> 00:23:08,021
Hi.

386
00:23:08,980 --> 00:23:09,896
Hey, Idhaya.

387
00:23:10,188 --> 00:23:12,812
Let's go. Boys are waiting
at the pitch to practice cricket.

388
00:23:12,813 --> 00:23:16,354
Hey, Juju has come here to meet me.

389
00:23:16,355 --> 00:23:17,605
He'll feel bad.

390
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:19,896
Yes, bro! Don't take him away.
I'll be bored.

391
00:23:21,646 --> 00:23:24,021
- Hey, Smack--
- Hey, let's go. Let's go.

392
00:23:26,188 --> 00:23:27,354
Switched off or not, I won.

393
00:23:27,355 --> 00:23:28,355
Why did you switch it off?

394
00:23:28,563 --> 00:23:30,312
You are always hanging out with him.

395
00:23:30,313 --> 00:23:31,896
You go away with him in the evening.

396
00:23:32,063 --> 00:23:33,520
Lately, you've been avoiding us.

397
00:23:33,521 --> 00:23:34,770
Why are you friends with a rowdy?

398
00:23:34,771 --> 00:23:36,146
Juju is my friend.

399
00:23:36,396 --> 00:23:38,146
Where do you both go every evening?

400
00:23:41,355 --> 00:23:43,063
Go, Juju, ride faster!

401
00:23:43,855 --> 00:23:45,771
Hey, we're late. Hurry up!

402
00:23:46,230 --> 00:23:47,480
Dude, why are you always late?

403
00:23:47,688 --> 00:23:49,062
That guy is grumpy. He'll yell at us.

404
00:23:49,063 --> 00:23:50,563
Live it up! We're the boys!

405
00:23:52,146 --> 00:23:53,771
Here, hold this! Let's go!

406
00:23:55,563 --> 00:23:57,230
- I'll go first!
- No, I'll go first!

407
00:24:24,355 --> 00:24:25,438
That's my shot!

408
00:24:25,563 --> 00:24:26,479
Yes!

409
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:27,771
Why is your girl standing idle?

410
00:24:28,021 --> 00:24:30,855
- Hey, Coach!
- Hey, why are you guys late?

411
00:24:32,230 --> 00:24:33,520
Sir, tire puncture.

412
00:24:33,521 --> 00:24:34,980
- Tire puncture, you say.
- Yes, sir.

413
00:24:35,188 --> 00:24:37,438
- Sir, were you plucking grass?
- No, sir.

414
00:24:37,605 --> 00:24:39,188
- That shot was really nice.
- Really?

415
00:24:40,313 --> 00:24:42,730
Son, eyes over here.

416
00:24:43,938 --> 00:24:45,104
I was observing the balls, sir.

417
00:24:45,105 --> 00:24:46,938
Wow! Observing balls?

418
00:24:47,230 --> 00:24:48,979
- Why not bat?
- Bat…

419
00:24:48,980 --> 00:24:50,063
- Bat, sir.
- Oh, you have it already.

420
00:24:50,313 --> 00:24:52,396
- No more coming late. Okay?
- Okay, sir.

421
00:24:53,688 --> 00:24:55,396
- Today's game went well.
- Yes!

422
00:24:55,938 --> 00:24:56,855
Thank you, Coach.

423
00:24:59,146 --> 00:25:00,355
- Bye-bye.
- Bye, Coach.

424
00:25:01,730 --> 00:25:02,646
Damn!

425
00:25:02,855 --> 00:25:03,771
The court is this way.

426
00:25:07,146 --> 00:25:08,812
Everyone is holding a book,
but you don't have one.

427
00:25:08,813 --> 00:25:10,312
We're not here to study.
I'll take one from him.

428
00:25:10,313 --> 00:25:11,146
Oh, no, my book!

429
00:25:13,605 --> 00:25:15,146
I'm happy I got to see my girl.

430
00:25:24,771 --> 00:25:26,271
I'm going to talk to her today.

431
00:25:26,396 --> 00:25:27,313
Thirty one.

432
00:25:29,355 --> 00:25:30,312
What is 31?

433
00:25:30,313 --> 00:25:32,187
You have told me 31 times
that you will speak to her.

434
00:25:32,188 --> 00:25:33,105
But you haven't till now.

435
00:25:33,355 --> 00:25:35,562
I feel confident today
that I'll speak to her.

436
00:25:35,563 --> 00:25:37,271
At least I will borrow
the focus guide from her.

437
00:25:39,771 --> 00:25:41,688
<i>Hey, come on, come here…</i>

438
00:25:41,855 --> 00:25:42,771
Juju!

439
00:25:43,313 --> 00:25:45,688
<i>Are you the gift fate gave me?</i>

440
00:25:48,688 --> 00:25:50,230
- It's over!
- 32.

441
00:25:53,188 --> 00:25:54,187
Come on! We'll do it tomorrow.

442
00:25:54,188 --> 00:25:55,895
Shut up! You're doing it on purpose.

443
00:25:55,896 --> 00:25:57,480
<i>Hey, come on, come here</i>

444
00:25:58,563 --> 00:26:00,730
<i>Are you the gift fate gave me?</i>

445
00:26:02,730 --> 00:26:05,646
Does anyone have a doubt about
Newton's Law, which we learned yesterday?

446
00:26:05,771 --> 00:26:06,688
Sir!

447
00:26:07,646 --> 00:26:10,187
Would you please also teach us
Newton's second law of motion?

448
00:26:10,188 --> 00:26:11,979
Good, this is what a good student is.

449
00:26:11,980 --> 00:26:13,271
No one else is asking a question.

450
00:26:13,396 --> 00:26:15,520
Imagine when we're cycling…

451
00:26:15,521 --> 00:26:17,605
I have an idea
to make our girls turn around.

452
00:26:17,855 --> 00:26:19,188
- What idea?
- Watch me.

453
00:26:19,855 --> 00:26:22,187
- Sir!
- Look, everyone is turning around.

454
00:26:22,188 --> 00:26:24,146
- I don't know anything.
- I don't know, either!

455
00:26:26,605 --> 00:26:28,355
- What is it?
- Sir, I have a doubt.

456
00:26:28,730 --> 00:26:29,688
What is your doubt?

457
00:26:29,938 --> 00:26:31,688
- Gautham asked you a doubt.
- Yes.

458
00:26:31,855 --> 00:26:33,730
If you explain it again,
it'll be helpful.

459
00:26:34,271 --> 00:26:36,313
If you could repeat Gautham's question…

460
00:26:36,646 --> 00:26:37,855
I will give you the answer.

461
00:26:39,146 --> 00:26:40,855
My doubt is cleared, sir.
It's cleared, sir.

462
00:26:40,980 --> 00:26:43,479
- It's clear. Absolutely cleared.
- Oh, clear?

463
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:44,729
He was asking for the sake of it.

464
00:26:44,730 --> 00:26:46,104
- So, you understood?
- Yes, sir.

465
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:47,771
Fine, now share with us.

466
00:26:48,521 --> 00:26:50,729
I understood, sir. I understood!

467
00:26:50,730 --> 00:26:52,312
- Okay.
- "Okay" is his answer.

468
00:26:52,313 --> 00:26:54,020
- Okay, sir.
- Sit down.

469
00:26:54,021 --> 00:26:55,354
Everyone turned around.

470
00:26:55,355 --> 00:26:57,188
Juju, you're amazing.

471
00:26:57,355 --> 00:26:58,480
It's a fantastic idea.

472
00:27:13,146 --> 00:27:15,313
Wondering why the coach is drinking cola?

473
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:17,355
How many of you like to drink cola?

474
00:27:17,521 --> 00:27:18,438
Sir, me! Me!

475
00:27:18,646 --> 00:27:19,563
So, all of you!

476
00:27:19,730 --> 00:27:20,730
Good! Good! Good! Good!

477
00:27:21,230 --> 00:27:23,355
So, this can is your target.

478
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:29,270
Now, you should serve to hit the target.

479
00:27:29,271 --> 00:27:32,438
Whoever fails to serve properly
will be served by me.

480
00:27:32,563 --> 00:27:33,480
Okay?

481
00:27:33,605 --> 00:27:36,145
Sir, how's that possible? The target
is quite far! Shall I bring it closer?

482
00:27:36,146 --> 00:27:37,896
What were you doing
all these days at practice?

483
00:27:38,230 --> 00:27:39,146
Now, serve!

484
00:27:39,313 --> 00:27:40,688
Aim at the bloody can.

485
00:27:45,813 --> 00:27:47,688
Why are you meddling with the balls?

486
00:27:48,063 --> 00:27:48,980
Come here!

487
00:27:51,938 --> 00:27:53,521
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

488
00:27:54,188 --> 00:27:58,105
Go to the women's court
and pick up balls.

489
00:28:01,188 --> 00:28:02,313
Okay, sir. Thank you.

490
00:28:03,563 --> 00:28:06,980
Why is he so happy about it?
Next, you!

491
00:28:09,646 --> 00:28:10,563
Juju!

492
00:28:11,938 --> 00:28:12,854
Now, you serve!

493
00:28:12,855 --> 00:28:14,437
If I miss,
will I be given the same punishment?

494
00:28:14,438 --> 00:28:16,021
You? Missing the target?

495
00:28:17,188 --> 00:28:18,896
- I have confidence in you, kid.
- Okay.

496
00:28:19,355 --> 00:28:21,021
Hail, Sania Mirza!

497
00:28:22,938 --> 00:28:25,146
Wow! Very good, my boy.

498
