Why are you separating the love pigeons?

739
00:40:58,896 --> 00:41:01,270
She's smiling.
Okay, I'll wrap them.

740
00:41:01,271 --> 00:41:02,230
Can I get sellotape?

741
00:41:02,771 --> 00:41:04,687
- Sellotape?
- Wait, let me check.

742
00:41:04,688 --> 00:41:06,020
I'll check.

743
00:41:06,021 --> 00:41:07,063
Check over there.

744
00:41:16,771 --> 00:41:17,688
Come on!

745
00:41:18,230 --> 00:41:19,146
Over there.

746
00:41:19,605 --> 00:41:20,605
I found it.

747
00:41:44,188 --> 00:41:46,355
Hey, what are you looking at?

748
00:41:46,646 --> 00:41:47,646
Are they twins?

749
00:41:47,938 --> 00:41:49,480
Yeah, they're twins!

750
00:41:54,188 --> 00:41:56,062
- Who was at the coaching class?
- Samantha.

751
00:41:56,063 --> 00:41:57,979
- Who was at the tennis class?
- Samyuktha.

752
00:41:57,980 --> 00:41:59,355
- Twins?
- Yeah!

753
00:41:59,521 --> 00:42:00,688
You didn't know?

754
00:42:00,813 --> 00:42:01,896
You're kidding, right?

755
00:42:02,146 --> 00:42:03,105
Hey, please shut up.

756
00:42:03,230 --> 00:42:04,771
- Juju?
- Idhaya, don't give her the gift.

757
00:42:04,896 --> 00:42:06,521
Give the CD to the girl
who came to the coaching class.

758
00:42:11,021 --> 00:42:12,980
How was the class today?

759
00:42:13,646 --> 00:42:15,313
Because of you,
I had to attend the coaching class.

760
00:42:15,688 --> 00:42:17,520
I did not study for the test.

761
00:42:17,521 --> 00:42:18,438
Hey, Dad is here.

762
00:42:19,980 --> 00:42:20,895
Shall we leave?

763
00:42:20,896 --> 00:42:23,188
<i>Happy birthday to you…</i>

764
00:42:27,063 --> 00:42:30,230
Hey, I told you many times
not to use my clothes.

765
00:42:30,521 --> 00:42:32,563
Likewise, don't touch my makeup.

766
00:42:32,688 --> 00:42:33,605
Get lost!

767
00:42:38,563 --> 00:42:42,729
This is the problem Juju hid behind
a rewritten question.

768
00:42:42,730 --> 00:42:43,646
Is it?

769
00:42:58,313 --> 00:43:01,605
Dude, you fell in love with the girl
who attended the coaching class.

770
00:43:02,063 --> 00:43:03,813
Moreover, it was she who noticed you.

771
00:43:04,146 --> 00:43:05,770
The girl who came to tennis class
ignored you.

772
00:43:05,771 --> 00:43:07,521
You propose to the girl
who came to the coaching class.

773
00:43:07,646 --> 00:43:08,937
That's the right thing to do.

774
00:43:08,938 --> 00:43:10,688
- He's right.
- Yes, dude, that'll be right to do.

775
00:43:12,563 --> 00:43:15,355
As you're twins
you guys must be having fun.

776
00:43:15,480 --> 00:43:18,480
We used to switch places
and attend coaching and tennis classes.

777
00:43:18,896 --> 00:43:21,230
How is it possible?
They could recognize you easily.

778
00:43:21,521 --> 00:43:23,063
You guys don't believe me, right?

779
00:43:23,230 --> 00:43:24,187
Wait!

780
00:43:24,188 --> 00:43:26,730
Juju, Idhaya, please come over here.

781
00:43:27,021 --> 00:43:28,938
Why is she calling me?
What's with her?

782
00:43:29,146 --> 00:43:30,313
Who's the coaching class Sam?

783
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:31,896
Identify who.

784
00:43:32,230 --> 00:43:33,604
Only today did we know they're twins.

785
00:43:33,605 --> 00:43:34,688
How do we identify her?

786
00:43:35,021 --> 00:43:35,938
Go ahead, give it a shot.

787
00:43:57,271 --> 00:44:00,480
Hey, Idhaya, I was the one who invited you
at the coaching class.

788
00:44:01,771 --> 00:44:04,938
See, I told you.
He won't be able to recognize.

789
00:44:07,688 --> 00:44:09,105
You girls are repeatedly hurting him.

790
00:44:28,271 --> 00:44:29,979
Are you single? Or twins?

791
00:44:29,980 --> 00:44:30,896
I'm not a twin.

792
00:44:31,188 --> 00:44:33,146
- But I'm committed.
- Hi, baby.

793
00:44:33,813 --> 00:44:34,730
Brother!

794
00:44:35,021 --> 00:44:36,687
- You were saying something.
- It's okay.

795
00:44:36,688 --> 00:44:38,354
Brother, I heard it.

796
00:44:38,355 --> 00:44:40,020
- Single and all…
- Let it go.

797
00:44:40,021 --> 00:44:41,562
Bro, it's okay to say it.

798
00:44:41,563 --> 00:44:43,937
Aren't you guys in a relationship?
Why are you nagging me?

799
00:44:43,938 --> 00:44:45,438
Annoying people
hurting us again and again.

800
00:45:05,730 --> 00:45:07,645
Idhaya! Idhaya!

801
00:45:07,646 --> 00:45:09,605
Hey, Idhaya, what happened?

802
00:45:10,730 --> 00:45:11,730
Open the door.

803
00:45:16,855 --> 00:45:18,771
Hey, Idhaya, say something.

804
00:45:22,063 --> 00:45:23,688
Hey, what happened?

805
00:45:32,896 --> 00:45:34,896
What happened to the guys
from those two benches?

806
00:45:35,355 --> 00:45:36,271
They are absent, sir.

807
00:45:40,771 --> 00:45:42,938
I don't know what to do after 5 p.m.

808
00:45:53,855 --> 00:45:56,688
<i>After that, I stopped going
to coaching and tennis to see her.</i>

809
00:45:56,813 --> 00:45:59,438
<i>Because I thought it was one,
but I fell for two girls.</i>

810
00:46:00,063 --> 00:46:02,146
<i>I'm clueless with whom I fell in love.</i>

811
00:46:02,688 --> 00:46:04,271
<i>I fell in love with only one girl.</i>

812
00:46:04,646 --> 00:46:05,646
<i>But I lost…</i>

813
00:46:09,563 --> 00:46:11,146
That's an interesting plot twist.

814
00:46:11,730 --> 00:46:13,146
Even Korean dramas couldn't compete.

815
00:46:13,480 --> 00:46:14,480
It's a new concept.

816
00:46:15,855 --> 00:46:17,355
Now, I'm laughing about it.

817
00:46:17,480 --> 00:46:19,230
Back then, it hurt me a lot.

818
00:46:20,855 --> 00:46:23,230
How did you manage
to fall in love again?

819
00:46:23,396 --> 00:46:26,313
Sir, do you know what the medicine
for love failure is?

820
00:46:26,563 --> 00:46:27,771
Is there a medicine for it?

821
00:46:28,021 --> 00:46:29,271
It's falling in love again.

822
00:46:30,646 --> 00:46:32,355
We moved to Chennai for our college.

823
00:46:32,855 --> 00:46:34,105
My uncle moved with us.

824
00:46:35,313 --> 00:46:37,980
<i>The days when we graduated
from college and had no jobs.</i>

825
00:46:38,105 --> 00:46:42,520
We're coming for a live telecast
on Thanga Uncle's terrace

826
00:46:42,521 --> 00:46:44,770
to watch the Cricket World Cup final.

827
00:46:44,771 --> 00:46:46,687
Dearest Sachin Tendulkar.

828
00:46:46,688 --> 00:46:48,855
Sweetheart Sehwag.
They're entering the pitch.

829
00:46:49,021 --> 00:46:50,771
Hey, I'm going to whack you.

830
00:46:50,980 --> 00:46:55,770
Priest, wait and watch, in the future,
Tamil commentary is going to be worse.

831
00:46:55,771 --> 00:46:57,062
And you'll be laughing at it.

832
00:46:57,063 --> 00:47:01,230
Hey, if they had employed our people,
they would've rocked it.

833
00:47:01,688 --> 00:47:03,313
Isn't cricket already
under your people's control?

834
00:47:03,521 --> 00:47:04,688
Please calm down.

835
00:47:08,188 --> 00:47:10,063
Uncle, you're something else, I say.

836
00:47:10,313 --> 00:47:12,562
You're telecasting the match on the
terrace and making tea in the kitchen.

837
00:47:12,563 --> 00:47:13,938
I wanted to watch the
match at the stadium.

838
00:47:14,105 --> 00:47:15,062
I couldn't get tickets.

839
00:47:15,063 --> 00:47:17,437
Also, I had saved some money
to watch the match.

840
00:47:17,438 --> 00:47:19,313
Since I couldn't make it to the stadium,

841
00:47:19,521 --> 00:47:21,395
I wanted to bring
the stadium atmosphere right here.

842
00:47:21,396 --> 00:47:22,895
So, I installed a screen upstairs.

843
00:47:22,896 --> 00:47:24,688
Venu, sentiment, is it?

844
00:47:25,521 --> 00:47:26,687
What sentiment?

845
00:47:26,688 --> 00:47:28,520
During the 1983 World Cup,

846
00:47:28,521 --> 00:47:30,354
Nallapadiandavar
stood with one leg just like this.

847
00:47:30,355 --> 00:47:31,688
He's following the same sentiment.

848
00:47:31,855 --> 00:47:33,395
Mr. Venu, don't put your leg down.

849
00:47:33,396 --> 00:47:35,437
If India wins the World Cup today…

850
00:47:35,438 --> 00:47:37,645
I'm going to order three big pots
of briyani from Charminar Briyani

851
00:47:37,646 --> 00:47:38,729
and give it as food donation.

852
00:47:38,730 --> 00:47:40,687
You'll be the first one to give
briyani as donation.

853
00:47:40,688 --> 00:47:42,480
- Are you serious?
- Yes!

854
00:47:43,021 --> 00:47:44,146
What's happening upstairs?

855
00:47:44,813 --> 00:47:47,605
You have installed a screen and
are telecasting the match like a movie.

856
00:47:48,271 --> 00:47:51,355
Don't you know you must inform
the Ward Councilor about it?

857
00:47:51,730 --> 00:47:54,229
After the 83's, only now
we're getting to see the World Cup.

858
00:47:54,230 --> 00:47:57,230
Even the Prime Minister is waiting
at the stadium to see them win.

859
00:47:57,355 --> 00:48:00,020
And you're here whining about the
clerk and the counselor. Oh, God!

860
00:48:00,021 --> 00:48:01,895
Even now, you won't invite me
to the match, right?

861
00:48:01,896 --> 00:48:03,604
Please come and watch.
Who's stopping you?

862
00:48:03,605 --> 00:48:05,812
The match is for everyone.
Please come and watch.

863
00:48:05,813 --> 00:48:06,812
Serve it to everyone.

864
00:48:06,813 --> 00:48:08,855
Hey, Uncle is here with the tea.
We can expect a sixer.

865
00:48:09,521 --> 00:48:10,437
Hey, move aside.

866
00:48:10,438 --> 00:48:12,938
Here comes Ghambir,
bowlers are going to tremble now.

867
00:48:13,438 --> 00:48:15,270
That's a fantastic straight drive.

868
00:48:15,271 --> 00:48:17,688
- Go and serve tea to everyone.
- First, you take a cup.

869
00:48:19,771 --> 00:48:21,480
Dear, are you seriously in love with him?

870
00:48:21,688 --> 00:48:23,605
Uncle, she might say no.
Please go and serve tea.

871
00:48:24,021 --> 00:48:24,938
A lot!

872
00:48:25,730 --> 00:48:27,480
Now this is what you call a match!

873
00:48:28,063 --> 00:48:30,562
- Here, have it.
<i>- You must not have beer on the roof top.</i>

874
00:48:30,563 --> 00:48:33,187
<i>The boss can't digest milk.</i>

875
00:48:33,188 --> 00:48:35,020
Do you have a pickle?
Pickle?

876
00:48:35,021 --> 00:48:37,688
Uncle, those goons are having booze.

877
00:48:37,980 --> 00:48:40,146
And they're asking for a pickle
to have with beer.

878
00:48:40,355 --> 00:48:43,854
It's wrong to have liquor
when women and children are around.

879
00:48:43,855 --> 00:48:45,980
And on top of it, you've asked
for pickles. Leave from here.

880
00:48:46,355 --> 00:48:48,020
How dare you remove us from here?

881
00:48:48,021 --> 00:48:49,855
- I ought to!
- How dare you lay your hands on us?

882
00:48:50,771 --> 00:48:51,980
Hey! Uncle! Uncle!

883
00:48:52,313 --> 00:48:55,437
Brother, why are you getting angry?
Watch the match!

884
00:48:55,438 --> 00:48:56,854
Hand me the bottle,
I'll put it in the fridge.

885
00:48:56,855 --> 00:48:58,813
Once India wins,
we'll have drinks together.

886
00:48:59,021 --> 00:49:00,021
You think India is going to win?

887
00:49:00,813 --> 00:49:01,771
My foot!

888
00:49:02,771 --> 00:49:04,438
<i>Hey, Sachin is out!</i>

889
00:49:04,980 --> 00:49:07,480
Gone! And they're expecting a win!

890
00:49:09,230 --> 00:49:11,230
As long as Dhoni is there,
the match won't end. Wait and watch.

891
00:49:11,355 --> 00:49:12,271
Dhoni…

892
00:49:13,605 --> 00:49:15,521
Brother, you can talk about us
all you want.

893
00:49:15,855 --> 00:49:17,145
But don't speak ill of Dhoni.

894
00:49:17,146 --> 00:49:19,188
Why? Is Dhoni a great player?

895
00:49:27,688 --> 00:49:31,063
<i>There go 4 runs!
And that's a fantastic shot.</i>

896
00:49:33,480 --> 00:49:37,354
<i>Left-hand batsmen hit
is flying towards the trophy.</i>

897
00:49:37,355 --> 00:49:39,188
<i>The fans are stunned by this shot.</i>

898
00:49:42,146 --> 00:49:44,271
<i>Is it going to Sri Lanka or India?</i>

899
00:49:44,396 --> 00:49:47,021
Bring it on!
Come on, come on!

900
00:49:47,230 --> 00:49:51,021
<i>Once again, Gautham Ghambir
delivered a fantastic shot.</i>

901
00:49:51,355 --> 00:49:52,979
<i>That was a fantastic shot.</i>

902
00:49:52,980 --> 00:49:55,062
<i>The ball hit the boundary,
and auntie here is yelling.</i>

903
00:49:55,063 --> 00:49:57,937
Hey, don't block the projector.
That's great, guys!

904
00:49:57,938 --> 00:49:58,854
Is this okay?

905
00:49:58,855 --> 00:50:01,688
<i>He got a gap
and has been scoring 4s continuously.</i>

906
00:50:01,813 --> 00:50:03,563
<i>Amazing game, I say.</i>

907
00:50:03,896 --> 00:50:10,063
<i>Virat Kohli is proving he's also in
this game by scoring boundaries.</i>

908
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:14,438
<i>Kohli's wicket was caught
like a goalie by Wilson.</i>

909
00:50:19,771 --> 00:50:23,730
<i>The champion batsman Yuvaraj Singh, of
this World Cup series, is coming to bat.</i>

910
00:50:24,188 --> 00:50:25,771
<i>That's a plot twist!</i>

911
00:50:40,896 --> 00:50:42,313
Idhaya, what happened?

912
00:50:42,438 --> 00:50:43,479
First, remove his shirt.

913
00:50:43,480 --> 00:50:45,479
- My eyes are burning.
- What happened?

914
00:50:45,480 --> 00:50:47,270
Bring out the vehicle.
We must take him to the hospital.

915
00:50:47,271 --> 00:50:48,938
- Hey, open your eyes.
- Idhaya! Idhaya!

916
00:50:50,730 --> 00:50:51,730
Buddy, watch out!

917
00:50:53,855 --> 00:50:55,480
Please have him sit carefully.

918
00:50:56,563 --> 00:50:57,730
Fire struck his eye, Doctor.

919
00:50:57,896 --> 00:50:59,688
Please check.
He's not able to open his eyes.

920
00:51:01,355 --> 00:51:02,855
Sir, please open your eyes slowly.

921
00:51:07,021 --> 00:51:08,396
I'm putting some drops.

922
00:51:08,521 --> 00:51:09,896
- He should be fine.
- Dude, is it burning?

923
00:51:11,146 --> 00:51:12,063
Of course!

924
00:51:13,563 --> 00:51:15,771
- Hey, check what the score is?
- Yeah, score!

925
00:51:17,355 --> 00:51:18,605
Look at him, Doctor.

926
00:51:18,771 --> 00:51:20,855
He's more concerned
about the match than his eyes.

927
00:51:20,980 --> 00:51:22,730
Hey, please calm down, dude.

928
00:51:22,938 --> 00:51:24,313
Hey, it's 224/4.

929
00:51:25,063 --> 00:51:26,687
- Where is Uncle?
- I don't know.

930
00:51:26,688 --> 00:51:27,605
Uncle!

931
00:51:50,355 --> 00:51:52,730
<i>And the score is 277/4!</i>

932
00:51:55,313 --> 00:51:58,146
<i>Everyone witnessed
Dhoni's winning shot on TV.</i>

933
00:51:58,563 --> 00:52:00,980
<i>But I witnessed it in her eyes.</i>

934
00:52:06,396 --> 00:52:08,480
Please follow these drops for two days.

935
00:52:09,230 --> 00:52:11,896
Don't make a wrong prescription
while celebrating India's victory.

936
00:52:13,063 --> 00:52:15,187
Hey, Ammu, India won!

937
00:52:15,188 --> 00:52:16,645
Dhoni scored a fantastic sixer
in the last ball.

938
00:52:16,646 --> 00:52:17,605
Why haven't you left yet?

939
00:52:19,980 --> 00:52:20,896
Sachin Bro!

940
00:52:21,771 --> 00:52:24,520
<i>I am ashamed
to call you guys my juniors.</i>

941
00:52:24,521 --> 00:52:25,479
<i>Damn!</i>

942
00:52:25,480 --> 00:52:28,313
- You became a doctor?
- What are you guys doing out here?

943
00:52:28,605 --> 00:52:29,855
This is what happened.

944
00:52:30,313 --> 00:52:32,813
When will you guys change?
Still starting fights everywhere.

945
00:52:33,146 --> 00:52:35,604
Brother, forget about it.
Why are you wearing a coat?

946
00:52:35,605 --> 00:52:37,354
- I'm a doctor.
- Doctor?

947
00:52:37,355 --> 00:52:39,855
Didn't you say kissing leads to pregnancy?
How did you become a doctor?

948
00:52:39,980 --> 00:52:41,063
It's not believable.

949
00:52:41,313 --> 00:52:42,938
Believe me. I'm a Doctor.

950
00:52:43,480 --> 00:52:45,687
Are you serious?
A doctor in our family.

951
00:52:45,688 --> 00:52:47,105
- I feel proud.
- Hey, take your hands off me.

952
00:52:47,813 --> 00:52:52,020
In fact, doctors are truly great.
They make a lot of sacrifices.

953
00:52:52,021 --> 00:52:53,646
- Yes, we work around the clock.
- Wow!

954
00:52:54,105 --> 00:52:56,896
- But as a doctor, everything--
- Hold it right there.

955
00:52:57,313 --> 00:52:58,395
You aren't so nice.

956
00:52:58,396 --> 00:53:00,312
- Why are you praising doctors now?
- Brother, you don't get me.

957
00:53:00,313 --> 00:53:01,646
- Sachin!
- It's a great profession--

958
00:53:02,146 --> 00:53:03,980
What are you doing?
It's getting late. Let's go.

959
00:53:04,563 --> 00:53:06,020
- Who is that, bro?
- My girlfriend.

960
00:53:06,021 --> 00:53:07,855
- Your girlfriend?
- Yeah!

961
00:53:07,980 --> 00:53:09,062
Stop lying to us.

962
00:53:09,063 --> 00:53:12,521
Hey, guys,
these people are my school juniors.

963
00:53:12,896 --> 00:53:14,770
- Hi!
- This is Lado, and this is Ammu.

964
00:53:14,771 --> 00:53:15,896
- Hi.
- And they're my college juniors.

965
00:53:16,813 --> 00:53:17,854
Hi!

966
00:53:17,855 --> 00:53:20,604
They don't believe me
that you're my girlfriend.

967
00:53:20,605 --> 00:53:22,230
- Is it?
- Yes!

968
00:53:22,605 --> 00:53:25,979
When you say a beautiful girl like me
is dating a guy like him,

969
00:53:25,980 --> 00:53:28,270
- people may find it hard to believe.
- Hey, that's enough!

970
00:53:28,271 --> 00:53:29,813
I was just kidding. Relax!

971
00:53:30,771 --> 00:53:32,271
Is your eye okay now?

972
00:53:32,813 --> 00:53:33,730
Much better!

973
00:53:34,438 --> 00:53:36,980
If the pain persists,
please come back tomorrow.

974
00:53:37,730 --> 00:53:38,646
Okay.

975
00:53:39,521 --> 00:53:41,146
I'm here to meet the girl I like.

976
00:53:42,355 --> 00:53:44,271
- My eyes are cured now.
- Yes!

977
00:53:46,688 --> 00:53:49,104
It won't be nice
if I don't bring her anything.

978
00:53:49,105 --> 00:53:52,938
Why don't you buy a rose
and a greeting card for her?

979
00:53:54,521 --> 00:53:56,605
- He's right!
- Hey! Get out of here!

980
00:53:57,021 --> 00:53:58,229
He's giving lame old ideas.

981
00:53:58,230 --> 00:53:59,770
- We'll do something new.
- Hey, the rose might--

982
00:53:59,771 --> 00:54:02,104
Rose, greeting card,
and gifting a pair of pigeons…

983
00:54:02,105 --> 00:54:04,188
It's all an old concept and is outdated.

984
00:54:04,396 --> 00:54:05,480
You must think fresh and trendy.

985
00:54:05,730 --> 00:54:06,812
I doubt following the trend…

986
00:54:06,813 --> 00:54:07,937
Brother, please help me out.

987
00:54:07,938 --> 00:54:10,188
She's in labor.
Please help me with her.

988
00:54:10,313 --> 00:54:12,355
- Don't think. It's an emergency.
- Why us?

989
00:54:12,521 --> 00:54:14,938
- Hey, let's check it out.
- Madam, bear a little, we're almost there.

990
00:54:15,730 --> 00:54:17,979
- Ma'am, watch your step.
- Someone, please help!

991
00:54:17,980 --> 00:54:19,854
Brother, bring out the gurney.

992
00:54:19,855 --> 00:54:21,438
Instead of waiting, you could carry her.

993
00:54:21,605 --> 00:54:23,563
- Please carry her.
- Hey, carry her!

994
00:54:25,230 --> 00:54:26,187
Don't be scared.

995
00:54:26,188 --> 00:54:27,980
- Watch out.
- Carry her.

996
00:54:28,230 --> 00:54:29,730
- Come on, carry her.
- This way.

997
00:54:29,855 --> 00:54:31,438
- Watch your step.
- Please be careful.

998
00:54:33,146 --> 00:54:34,480
Brother, come along.

999
00:54:34,855 --> 00:54:37,980
Brother, it's not always necessary
for an auto driver to help during labor.

1000
00:54:38,188 --> 00:54:40,229
- You too can help her.
- Get lost!

1001
00:54:40,230 --> 00:54:42,104
Dude, you thought
you didn't get her anything.

1002
00:54:42,105 --> 00:54:43,605
But God has graced you with a huge gift.

1003
00:54:44,146 --> 00:54:45,937
Hey, ask which way the labor ward is.

1004
00:54:45,938 --> 00:54:47,521
- Doctor! Over here.
- Careful.

1005
00:54:47,646 --> 00:54:49,521
- She's in labor pain. Check on her.
- It's an emergency.

1006
00:54:50,813 --> 00:54:52,063
Her pulse is high.

1007
00:54:52,480 --> 00:54:53,895
- Where's the gurney?
- No need for that.

1008
00:54:53,896 --> 00:54:55,563
Bring her over to that room.

1009
00:54:56,855 --> 00:54:58,521
Careful! Careful! Slowly.

1010
00:55:01,563 --> 00:55:04,479
- Nurse, quickly check her blood pressure.
- Yes, Doctor.

1011
00:55:04,480 --> 00:55:05,771
Don't worry. You'll be fine.

1012
00:55:05,980 --> 00:55:08,270
- Nurse, prep for the procedure.
- You're okay. Doing great!

1013
00:55:08,271 --> 00:55:10,604
- Let's go.
- Check if we have all the medicines.

1014
00:55:10,605 --> 00:55:12,438
- Why are you still standing over there?
- Sir?

1015
00:55:13,396 --> 00:55:16,854
How long are men going to keep avoiding
being by their wives' side during labor?

1016
00:55:16,855 --> 00:55:19,188
Go and witness the struggle
she's going through.

1017
00:55:19,355 --> 00:55:22,020
- Oh, no, you have got it wrong.
- It's wrong. Come with me.

1018
00:55:22,021 --> 00:55:23,729
- Nurse, I'm not her husband--
- Come on!

1019
00:55:23,730 --> 00:55:24,980
- Please hear me out.
- Go inside!

1020
00:55:26,605 --> 00:55:28,188
Turn around. Wear this.

1021
00:55:28,605 --> 00:55:30,104
Is this your first pregnancy?

1022
00:55:30,105 --> 00:55:33,188
Previous pregnancy, C-section,
or any complications?

1023
00:55:33,355 --> 00:55:35,355
What's her blood group? A, B, O?

1024
00:55:36,021 --> 00:55:38,480
- Any allergies?
- Yeah, she sneezed on her way here.

1025
00:55:39,730 --> 00:55:42,188
- When did she go into labor?
- The vehicle just arrived.

1026
00:55:42,396 --> 00:55:44,230
- I'm asking about labor pains.
- Don't worry. You'll be fine.

1027
00:55:44,980 --> 00:55:45,896
Bend down.

1028
00:55:46,563 --> 00:55:48,105
He does not know anything!

1029
00:55:48,605 --> 00:55:51,188
- Hurry up! I can't bear the pain.
- It's okay.

1030
00:55:51,771 --> 00:55:54,271
- Nurse, quickly prep the delivery tray.
- It's ready.

1031
00:55:54,521 --> 00:55:56,730
Bloody man,
how could you not know anything?

1032
00:55:56,896 --> 00:55:58,812
This pregnant lady's
curse won't spare you.

1033
00:55:58,813 --> 00:56:00,271
Go and give her some courage.

1034
00:56:00,855 --> 00:56:01,980
Go ahead, man!

1035
00:56:02,105 --> 00:56:04,063
Hello! Please be brave.

1036
00:56:04,230 --> 00:56:06,270
- Please be brave.
- Hold his hand.

1037
00:56:06,271 --> 00:56:07,230
Hold it tight!

1038
00:56:08,271 --> 00:56:10,021
- Please be brave.
- I'm on my way, Doctor.

1039
00:56:10,271 --> 00:56:12,771
- Be brave.
- Push, push. You can do it.

1040
00:56:12,896 --> 00:56:13,812
Take a deep breath.

1041
00:56:13,813 --> 00:56:16,020
- Doctor, she's fully dilated.
- Okay.

1042
00:56:16,021 --> 00:56:17,813
- Push! Push!
- You can do it!

1043
00:56:17,938 --> 00:56:19,812
Come on. Come on.
One more push.

1044
00:56:19,813 --> 00:56:21,646
Why do you have your back
turned to your wife?

1045
00:56:31,563 --> 00:56:33,521
- Something is not right.
- You're right!

1046
00:56:34,063 --> 00:56:35,770
A woman comes in an auto in labor.

1047
00:56:35,771 --> 00:56:37,480
And he'll carry her to the ward.

1048
00:56:37,813 --> 00:56:40,020
And he stays back during the labor.

1049
00:56:40,021 --> 00:56:40,938
I can't believe it.

1050
00:56:41,313 --> 00:56:43,688
- Very wrong!
- He's always been this person.

1051
00:56:43,813 --> 00:56:45,688
Right! When he was 10,
he signed for his teacher.

1052
00:56:46,230 --> 00:56:49,854
Hey, why didn't you tell them
you're not her husband?

1053
00:56:49,855 --> 00:56:51,355
They never let me speak.

1054
00:56:51,646 --> 00:56:53,146
Moreover, her husband wasn't with her.

1055
00:56:54,146 --> 00:56:55,771
I felt very bad for her.

1056
00:56:59,105 --> 00:57:01,105
Mom would've struggled
the same way, right?

1057
00:57:01,230 --> 00:57:03,146
Hey, it's a comedy scene.

1058
00:57:03,480 --> 00:57:04,813
Don't turn it into
a mother-sentiment scene.

1059
00:57:05,730 --> 00:57:07,063
Do you think
Amudha would've misunderstood me?

1060
00:57:07,813 --> 00:57:09,896
Sounds like Idhaya likes her a lot.

1061
00:57:11,021 --> 00:57:12,355
Nothing like that.

1062
00:57:13,146 --> 00:57:15,354
I couldn't get you married
to the girl you like.

1063
00:57:15,355 --> 00:57:17,563
But do you think
I wouldn't know who you like?

1064
00:57:22,313 --> 00:57:24,063
Why is she calling me now?
Hello?

1065
00:57:25,605 --> 00:57:26,521
Oh, no!

1066
00:57:27,521 --> 00:57:29,646
What are you saying? Where?

1067
00:57:31,438 --> 00:57:32,438
I'll be right there!

1068
00:57:34,980 --> 00:57:35,896
What happened?

1069
00:57:38,021 --> 00:57:40,771
- What happened?
- Lado and Amudha have no other business.

1070
00:57:40,980 --> 00:57:43,605
They got caught by the traffic police.
Ignore it!

1071
00:57:45,021 --> 00:57:46,646
What are you saying?
Let's help them.

1072
00:57:46,896 --> 00:57:50,313
Basically, when girls get caught and cry,
they let them go.

1073
00:57:50,813 --> 00:57:53,396
But our women are arrogant to the max.

1074
00:57:53,646 --> 00:57:55,896
They would've run their mouth.
And got caught.

1075
00:57:56,021 --> 00:57:57,146
Bro, Amudha is out there.

1076
00:57:57,688 --> 00:57:59,021
Uncle, make him understand.

1077
00:57:59,396 --> 00:58:01,645
Yes, you guys carry on.
I'll take care of the booze.

1078
00:58:01,646 --> 00:58:03,980
- I'll take care of Uncle.
- Didn't you say we must help others?

1079
00:58:04,105 --> 00:58:05,855
Now what? Only if you
come along will others follow.

1080
00:58:05,980 --> 00:58:06,896
Please, come with me.

1081
00:58:07,271 --> 00:58:10,145
- He's a nuisance.
- Sachin, even the police would spare them.

1082
00:58:10,146 --> 00:58:11,605
But he won't spare us.
Let's get them.

1083
00:58:12,021 --> 00:58:13,980
- Hey, Idhaya, let's go after this drink.
- Let's go!

1084
00:58:14,605 --> 00:58:17,770
Lately, women get drunk
and cause a ruckus.

1085
00:58:17,771 --> 00:58:19,188
- Yes, sir.
- Hey, Policeman!

1086
00:58:19,396 --> 00:58:21,687
Do you think drinking alcohol
is only men's right?

1087
00:58:21,688 --> 00:58:23,313
- Stop talking nonsense!
- Please shut up.

1088
00:58:28,605 --> 00:58:30,270
- No one gets out of the car.
- Okay, dude.

1089
00:58:30,271 --> 00:58:31,396
Everyone, wait here.

1090
00:58:32,438 --> 00:58:33,855
Please stop talking.

1091
00:58:34,063 --> 00:58:35,646
How could he speak so disrespectfully?

1092
00:58:35,771 --> 00:58:37,312
How dare he say whatever he wants?

1093
00:58:37,313 --> 00:58:39,479
Hello, how dare you call me a dog!

1094
00:58:39,480 --> 00:58:42,438
I won't insult the dogs
by comparing them to you.

1095
00:58:43,813 --> 00:58:45,354
- Lado, please--
- What happened?

1096
00:58:45,355 --> 00:58:46,895
Look, he's going overboard.

1097
00:58:46,896 --> 00:58:48,896
- Please calm down for a minute.
- Where's Sachin? Call him.

1098
00:58:49,146 --> 00:58:50,396
Lado, please calm down for a moment.

1099
00:58:50,855 --> 00:58:51,771
What happened?

1100
00:58:51,896 --> 00:58:53,437
I was driving the car.

1101
00:58:53,438 --> 00:58:56,521
They checked and asked me to go.
But she spoke out of turn.

1102
00:58:56,896 --> 00:58:59,770
This police officer
looks like trouble to me.

1103
00:58:59,771 --> 00:59:02,187
- Yes!
- Oh, she's a doctor, is she?

1104
00:59:02,188 --> 00:59:04,355
That doesn't give her the right
to speak down to the police.

1105
00:59:04,480 --> 00:59:05,480
How could she call me a dog?

1106
00:59:05,688 --> 00:59:07,813
- Sir, please forgive them.
- Why should I listen to you?

1107
00:59:07,938 --> 00:59:10,980
- Get to the side.
- Sir, I know my rules.

1108
00:59:11,313 --> 00:59:12,605
Only the co-passenger was drunk.

1109
00:59:12,896 --> 00:59:14,771
The driver wasn't drunk.
Why are you holding them?

1110
00:59:14,896 --> 00:59:16,813
Talking rules, is it? Super!

1111
00:59:17,105 --> 00:59:18,437
- Sir, please understand…
- Sir! Sir!

1112
00:59:18,438 --> 00:59:20,105
- Sir!
- What's the issue?

1113
00:59:20,271 --> 00:59:22,271
Sir, it's a DD case.
I'm investigating, sir.

1114
00:59:23,230 --> 00:59:26,104
Sir, only the co-passenger was drunk.
The driver wasn't drunk.

1115
00:59:26,105 --> 00:59:27,563
They're causing unnecessary problems.

1116
00:59:27,688 --> 00:59:30,438
Sir, he's distracting you.
Don't believe him.

1117
00:59:30,730 --> 00:59:32,646
Hey, stay normal.

1118
00:59:32,938 --> 00:59:33,855
Sir.

1119
00:59:34,605 --> 00:59:36,313
You've become a nuisance lately.

1120
00:59:37,313 --> 00:59:38,855
- Send them away.
- Thank you, sir.

1121
00:59:41,605 --> 00:59:42,521
Get in, let's go.

1122
00:59:43,438 --> 00:59:44,855
Lado, get inside the car.

1123
00:59:45,771 --> 00:59:47,395
Super! Idhaya solved the issue.

1124
00:59:47,396 --> 00:59:51,480
Hey, did you see my nephew?
He smartly handled the situation.

1125
00:59:51,605 --> 00:59:53,896
Smart, my foot!
Who's going to drive us home?

1126
00:59:54,688 --> 00:59:57,145
- Yes! Who's going to drive us?
- Is my mouth stinking?

1127
00:59:57,146 --> 00:59:58,813
- It's not stinking.
- Not at all, Uncle.

1128
00:59:58,938 --> 01:00:01,438
Now we've become friends of the police.
I'll drive.

1129
01:00:02,646 --> 01:00:04,730
Come on, drive, Uncle.

1130
01:00:05,271 --> 01:00:07,605
Uncle, we should arrive home
before they do.

1131
01:00:07,938 --> 01:00:09,105
Watch me drive now!

1132
01:00:13,271 --> 01:00:14,770
- Hey, ask them to leave.
- Leave!

1133
01:00:14,771 --> 01:00:16,438
- Leave!
- Drive, Uncle.

1134
01:00:16,563 --> 01:00:20,270
- Don't you know who we are?
- Uncle, why are you bringing it up?

1135
01:00:20,271 --> 01:00:22,520
- The gang that went before us…
- Yes!

1136
01:00:22,521 --> 01:00:23,563
…we're part of the same gang.

1137
01:00:24,521 --> 01:00:26,313
- He's a doctor.
- His tattoo says it too.

1138
01:00:27,021 --> 01:00:28,771
There's a sticker that says so, too.

1139
01:00:28,938 --> 01:00:29,896
Sir, there's a sticker.

1140
01:00:30,063 --> 01:00:31,563
A sticker doesn't prove
that you're a doctor.

1141
01:00:31,980 --> 01:00:34,396
Why is everyone
announcing themselves as doctors?

1142
01:00:34,521 --> 01:00:36,145
How dare you
sit inside the car disrespectfully?

1143
01:00:36,146 --> 01:00:37,062
Step out of the car.

1144
01:00:37,063 --> 01:00:39,312
Why would you get us into trouble, uncle?
Step out!

1145
01:00:39,313 --> 01:00:40,730
Step out of the car.

1146
01:00:50,188 --> 01:00:51,730
- Is he a doctor?
- Exactly, sir.

1147
01:00:51,896 --> 01:00:53,480
I think he doesn't believe you.

1148
01:00:54,146 --> 01:00:55,688
Say a few medicine names aloud.

1149
01:00:57,813 --> 01:01:02,021
Anacin, Crocin, Dolo
650, and Azithromycin.

1150
01:01:03,438 --> 01:01:04,854
See, he's a doctor.

1151
01:01:04,855 --> 01:01:09,937
Vicks Action 500, Paracetamol,
Vicks, Halls, Strepsils.

1152
01:01:09,938 --> 01:01:11,354
- Are you a doctor too?
- Halls?

1153
01:01:11,355 --> 01:01:13,146
Then how did you end up
in the police department?

1154
01:01:13,271 --> 01:01:15,770
Hey! Even a grocery store owner
can list these medicines.

1155
01:01:15,771 --> 01:01:18,229
Naming these medicines won't prove
you're a doctor. Get inside the car.

1156
01:01:18,230 --> 01:01:20,605
- Come on, let's go!
- Hey, where are you going?

1157
01:01:20,730 --> 01:01:21,645
Get inside this car.

1158
01:01:21,646 --> 01:01:22,895
- This one?
- Get inside this vehicle.

1159
01:01:22,896 --> 01:01:24,313
- Come on, get inside.
- Oh, no…

1160
01:01:24,896 --> 01:01:25,813
Come in!

1161
01:01:28,480 --> 01:01:30,396
Welcome home!

1162
01:01:31,646 --> 01:01:33,980
- Would you like to have something?
- What's this mess?

1163
01:01:34,188 --> 01:01:36,396
We got caught by the police

1164
01:01:36,563 --> 01:01:39,396
but you guys here were
chilling and boozing.

1165
01:01:40,355 --> 01:01:41,438
- Hey, calm down.
<i>- Dude.</i>

1166
01:01:41,730 --> 01:01:43,437
- Dude, we got caught by the police.
- Hey, Lado!

1167
01:01:43,438 --> 01:01:45,105
- Can you hear me?
<i>- Hello! Hello!</i>

1168
01:01:45,230 --> 01:01:46,562
<i>- Can you hear me?</i>
- Yes, I can. Tell me.

1169
01:01:46,563 --> 01:01:48,355
Who's it? Is it Sachin?

1170
01:01:48,730 --> 01:01:50,645
Give it to me.
Hello! What happened?

1171
01:01:50,646 --> 01:01:53,479
We trusted Uncle to drive
and got caught by the police.

1172
01:01:53,480 --> 01:01:55,980
- Who's speaking?
- Aww, so sad!

1173
01:01:56,355 --> 01:01:57,355
- So sad!
<i>- Yes, baby!</i>

1174
01:01:57,521 --> 01:01:58,688
You'd better rot out there.

1175
01:01:58,813 --> 01:02:00,438
What did you tell me
when I called you for help?

1176
01:02:00,563 --> 01:02:03,396
- Hey, hey, babe!
- Don't say anything.

1177
01:02:03,938 --> 01:02:05,729
- Don't you call yourself a boyfriend.
- Dad's calling.

1178
01:02:05,730 --> 01:02:06,812
Your dad?

1179
01:02:06,813 --> 01:02:09,480
- Go to the roof top and talk.
- I noticed empty bottles here.

1180
01:02:09,730 --> 01:02:12,396
- Baby, please send someone to help.
- Who are you talking to?

1181
01:02:13,855 --> 01:02:14,771
Give me the phone.

1182
01:02:15,938 --> 01:02:17,980
<i>- Be careful, dear.</i>
- Okay, Dad.

1183
01:02:18,813 --> 01:02:20,354
<i>Please eat on time and sleep.</i>

1184
01:02:20,355 --> 01:02:21,313
Please go to sleep.

1185
01:02:21,480 --> 01:02:22,396
<i>Sure, dear!</i>

1186
01:02:22,771 --> 01:02:23,937
I'm going to sleep now.

1187
01:02:23,938 --> 01:02:25,480
- Lado?
- She slept.

1188
01:02:25,855 --> 01:02:28,021
<i>- Take care.</i>
- I'll call you in the morning.

1189
01:02:28,188 --> 01:02:30,563
<i>- Okay, dear.</i>
- Okay, bye, Dad.

1190
01:02:34,313 --> 01:02:35,230
It was Dad.

1191
01:02:35,730 --> 01:02:38,938
Asking about my
whereabouts and activities.

1192
01:02:39,480 --> 01:02:42,771
He takes care of me like I'm a child.

1193
01:02:46,063 --> 01:02:47,146
How about your family?

1194
01:02:47,855 --> 01:02:49,480
No issues in my family.

1195
01:02:49,771 --> 01:02:52,063
It's always fun for sons.

1196
01:02:52,396 --> 01:02:53,355
That's not the case.

1197
01:02:54,105 --> 01:02:55,688
I don't have parents.

1198
01:02:57,855 --> 01:02:58,855
I'm sorry, Idhaya.

1199
01:02:59,438 --> 01:03:01,396
It's okay. I have my Uncle.

1200
01:03:02,605 --> 01:03:04,896
He's equal to a hundred parents.
He's great at it!

1201
01:03:10,896 --> 01:03:12,771
What's this DTV?

1202
01:03:14,521 --> 01:03:15,980
Oh, this?

1203
01:03:16,271 --> 01:03:17,771
It's our local cable TV channel.

1204
01:03:17,938 --> 01:03:20,355
My Uncle and I dream of
making that into a satellite channel.

1205
01:03:20,605 --> 01:03:22,563
- Super!
- Thanks!

1206
01:03:27,855 --> 01:03:28,980
Would you like to have something?

1207
01:03:29,896 --> 01:03:30,813
No!

1208
01:03:32,021 --> 01:03:33,563
Can I get a simple cup of tea?

1209
01:03:34,105 --> 01:03:36,855
Not sure about a simple cup of tea, but
I can get you the best tea in the world.

1210
01:03:37,355 --> 01:03:38,355
Would you adjust?

1211
01:03:39,896 --> 01:03:41,896
- Okay.
- I'll bring it.

1212
01:03:52,688 --> 01:03:53,605
How's it?

1213
01:03:56,063 --> 01:03:58,896
What's the special ingredient
of the world's best tea?

1214
01:04:00,105 --> 01:04:01,605
<i>Add tea powder to boiling water.</i>

1215
01:04:01,730 --> 01:04:04,938
<i>Then add a piece of ginger
and sprinkle Tulasi over it.</i>

1216
01:04:05,146 --> 01:04:07,688
<i>Finally, add lots of love…</i>

1217
01:04:07,980 --> 01:04:10,188
If you have this tea, you won't forget
its taste for the rest of your life.

1218
01:04:13,188 --> 01:04:15,271
You added a lot of ingredients,
but did you add sugar?

1219
01:04:16,480 --> 01:04:17,396
Sugar?

1220
01:04:23,063 --> 01:04:24,771
Shall I add sugar and bring it back?

1221
01:04:25,646 --> 01:04:27,355
It's okay.
I'm liking this taste.

1222
01:04:28,688 --> 01:04:29,605
Sorry.

1223
01:04:34,396 --> 01:04:37,896
From now on, every cup of tea
will remind me of this one.

1224
01:04:38,188 --> 01:04:40,021
- You mean this sugarless tea?
- Yes!

1225
01:05:11,855 --> 01:05:15,688
<i>With dreams in tow,
I came to tell a story</i>

1226
01:05:15,855 --> 01:05:19,521
<i>With memories lingering,
I stood in a different hue</i>

1227
01:05:19,771 --> 01:05:23,396
<i>Through you,
I saw miracles beyond reality</i>

1228
01:05:23,605 --> 01:05:27,063
<i>You made me feel happiness
Unknown to me</i>

1229
01:05:27,313 --> 01:05:30,896
<i>The heavens, vast and infinite…</i>

1230
01:05:31,146 --> 01:05:34,480
<i>Won't a tender drizzle grace me?</i>

1231
01:05:34,605 --> 01:05:38,813
<i>And in it…</i>

1232
01:05:38,980 --> 01:05:42,771
<i>My soul yearns to be drenched too</i>

1233
01:05:43,105 --> 01:05:46,938
<i>Where friendship thrives, sorrow fades
The heart carries no weight</i>

1234
01:05:47,271 --> 01:05:50,813
<i>The path unfolds in bloom
When you're by my side</i>

1235
01:05:50,938 --> 01:05:54,771
<i>No path is found unfelt
No love exists unbroken</i>

1236
01:05:54,896 --> 01:05:58,355
<i>No scar is too deep
When it belongs to the tale</i>

